course: dictionary
lesson: 12459
title: Deferral: putting it off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deferral is when something is put off until a later time. It is a formal word, so you will mostly see it in letters from schools, universities, banks and governments. «The school granted Maya a deferral, so she could start university next year.» Maya did not lose her place. It was just moved to later.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like «ask for», «granted» and «next year» help you work out the meaning. Try swapping in "a delay that is allowed" and see if the sentence still makes sense. It does, so you know you have it right.
explain: A deferral is close to a delay, but it is usually official and agreed. A delay can just happen, like a late bus. «The bank agreed to a deferral of my loan payment for three months.» The bank said yes to waiting, so the payment is not cancelled.
fact: Deferral means putting something off until a later time.
fact: A deferral is often official, which means someone in charge has agreed to it.
fact: «Deferral» is a noun, and its plural is «deferrals».
fact: Phrases you might see are «ask for a deferral», «grant a deferral» and «a deferral of payment».
fact: A deferral is not a cancellation: the thing still happens, just later.
exercise: «The college granted Tom a deferral, so he could start in September.» What does deferral mean here? | Cancelling his place for good | A prize for working hard | *Permission to start later | A fast train to the city
exercise: «Sara asked the bank for a deferral on her card payment.» What did Sara ask for? | A new card that is free for ever | *A delay in paying | More money to spend | A meeting with the manager tomorrow
exercise: The school sent a letter about the deferral of the trip. What does this tell you? | The trip is free | The trip is cancelled for ever | The trip has already happened | *The trip is put off until a later time
test: «The government granted a deferral of the tax bill until next spring.» What does this mean? | *The bill is put off until spring | The tax was cancelled completely | The bill went to a different office | The bill was paid early in winter
test: Which word means a delay that someone in charge has officially agreed to? | *A deferral | A lost letter | A late bus | A sudden stop
exam: Mia reads, «Your deferral of entry has been approved.» What has happened? | Mia has been thrown out of the school | Mia has been moved to a new town | Mia has finished the course early | *Mia has permission to start the course later
